WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.650
Here's the idea the
whole appendix rests on.

2
00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:06.533
A ticket that sends a person to
a console doesn't prove anything;

3
00:00:06.533 --> 00:00:08.325
it just changes who's to blame.

4
00:00:08.325 --> 00:00:13.088
The person does the work, replies
"done," and the record holds a claim.

5
00:00:13.088 --> 00:00:17.088
Now flip it: the person approves,
a machine runs a versioned

6
00:00:17.088 --> 00:00:21.088
plan under its own identity,
and a re-read proves the result.

7
00:00:21.088 --> 00:00:25.275
The person keeps the one job a
machine can't do, which is to decide.

8
00:00:25.275 --> 00:00:28.476
And this matters because a
platform that finds drift

9
00:00:28.476 --> 00:00:32.113
perfectly but closes it slowly
is just documenting neglect.

10
00:00:32.113 --> 00:00:34.660
So what does the machine
path look like end to end?
